This file exists solely so `mailosh/web/static/` is present on a fresh
clone. `mailosh/web/app.py`'s `StaticFiles(directory=...)` mount raises
`RuntimeError` at import/test-collection time if this directory doesn't
exist at all -- the vendored JS (`vendor/`) and built CSS (`app.css`) that
actually belong here are gitignored and fetched/built by `make vendor`/
`make css` (also run automatically by `make test`/`make itest`/`make up`;
see the top-level Makefile and README).
